invariant: INV-14
file: cpu.h
catches: webpki_session_host
reason: cpu_value_ok stops refusing a bit the object does not define, so a
  bit a later release adds runs as though this object knew what it says.
  The ruling is that such a bit is refused, not ignored
  (docs/decisions.md 89). test/webpki_session_cpu.h requires ch_connect
  to refuse the first bit past CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA and the top bit.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_PROBED) != 0 && (cpu & ~(uint32_t)CH_CPU_DEFINED) == 0;
--- new
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_PROBED) != 0;
